course: dictionary
lesson: 9821
title: Sweet: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, so the context tells you which one to use. Ask yourself: what does the sentence describe? «On a sunny day a honeybee drinks sweet nectar from a flower.» Nectar is food, so sweet means tasting like sugar or honey.
explain: In the UK, «sweets» are candies, and one candy is a sweet. A sweet can also be a dessert, the pudding at the end of a meal. Check the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: Sweet can describe a person or a feeling too. «She gave me a sweet smile.» A smile is not something you taste, so sweet means kind and gentle here.
fact: Sweet is an adjective: sweet, sweeter, sweetest.
fact: «Sweets» is a plural noun; one candy is «a sweet» (UK).
fact: «Sweet» means tasting like sugar or honey.
fact: «Sweet» can also mean kind and gentle, or pleasant and cute: «a sweet puppy».
fact: Boiled sweets are made by boiling sugar syrup until almost all the water is gone, so they set hard and glassy.
exercise: «On a sunny day a honeybee drinks sweet nectar from a flower.» What does sweet mean here? | Kind and gentle | *Tasting like sugar or honey | Very loud | Pleasant and cute
exercise: In the UK, what is one sweet? | A bee | *A candy | A festival | A lamp
exercise: «She gave me a sweet smile.» What does sweet mean here? | *Kind and gentle | Tasting like honey | Very loud | Hard and glassy
test: «After the meal, the waiter brought the sweet.» What is the sweet? | *A dessert at the end of a meal | A bee | A lamp | A candy
test: Which phrase means tasting like sugar or honey? | a kind, sweet smile | a sweet puppy | *a sweet honey cake | a sweet dream
exam: Maths: you share 12 sweets equally between 3 children. How many does each child get? | 6 | 3 | *4 | 9
